From 74d6741a11f0f942fa029e9a699096e68a1f30b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 22:07:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: the first-boot box isolates its fields from browser
 autofill, prefills nothing, lowercases the login name and ends in the
 REBOOTING screen

GT-BE98 field report after a factory reset: with Chrome's autocompletion on
"Router Login Name" the Wi-Fi password was set to the saved router login
password, and "Set up and restart Wi-Fi" showed an update widget for a few
seconds and then reloaded the page while the router went down.

- One <form> wrapped the whole box, and a browser pairs a saved login with the
  first visible password field in the same form - the Wi-Fi password. The
  start_apply form now wraps only the credential fields; the Wi-Fi inputs are
  formless and reach the box through reaper_wifisetup.cgi alone. wifi_psk and
  http_passwd_x carry autocomplete="new-password", the current-password field
  "current-password".
- Nothing is prepopulated: the login name starts empty (it came from nvram).
- The router login name is lowercase only: folded as typed (lowerLogin, caret
  kept) and validated with a lowercase regex.
- action_wait was 0, so start_apply.htm in the hidden frame redirected the top
  window back to this page as soon as nvram was committed. It is now the
  model's reboot time (what the shell's rebootForm sends), the page shows the
  shell's REBOOTING overlay (same tokens and colours) with a countdown, then
  polls /httpd_check.xml and lands on "/" when httpd answers; the hidden frame
  is dropped once its reply has loaded, so its own redirect can never fire.
- Button: RWFS_8 = "Apply & Reboot" in all 25 packs.

Gate: reaper_static_checks check_firstboot_wifi asserts the form order, the two
new-password inputs, no nvram-prefilled login name, lowerLogin + the lowercase
regex, action_wait = reboot time and the overlay; six verify_markers lines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
