 	A refused password stops everything; a refused Wi-Fi setting still persists
 	the password change so the box is never left half-done.
 
+	v3.3.2 (GT-BE98 field report): (1) the Wi-Fi inputs live OUTSIDE the credential
+	form. Chrome pairs a saved login with the first visible password field in the
+	same form - which was the Wi-Fi password - so picking a saved router login
+	silently set the Wi-Fi key to the router password. The start_apply form now
+	wraps only the credential fields; the Wi-Fi fields reach the box through the
+	CGI alone. Both new-password fields carry autocomplete="new-password".
+	(2) Nothing is prepopulated: the login name starts empty (placeholder only).
+	(3) The login name is lowercase-only - lowercased as typed, rejected otherwise.
+	(4) After "Apply & Reboot" the page shows the shell's REBOOTING overlay
+	(same look as the GUI's Reboot: title, countdown, note), counts the model's
+	reboot time down, then polls /httpd_check.xml and lands on "/". The form's
+	action_wait is the model's reboot time (was 0, so the hidden frame's own
+	redirect bounced the user back to this page within seconds), and the frame
+	is removed once its reply has arrived so it can never pull the page back.
+
 	i18n: RWFS_* tokens (English-seeded, 25 packs) plus reused stock tokens.
 	Tokens appear only in double-quoted or backtick JS strings (rule 29) and in
 	HTML text. ASCII only (rule 1). Rendered with the reaper theme via
